  "goodToKnow": "Die Hansestadt is a Hanseatic city, a member of die Hanse, the medieval trading league that dominated the Baltic and North Sea from the 13th to the 17th century, led by Lübeck. Hamburg and Bremen still call themselves Freie Hansestadt, hence the number plates HH (Hansestadt Hamburg) and HB, and Rostock has HRO. Hanseatisch describes a reserved, understated, honourable style. Lufthansa takes its name from it. Plural: die Hansestädte."
